  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Concerned though with the deteriorating macroeconomic situation and the importance of supporting businesses, particularly SMEs and key sectors, in May 2020 FCEF undertook a rapid impact assessment of COVID-19 on member enterprises reaching 67 enterprises across 8 districts in Fiji &#x2013; the first enterprise-based COVID impact study in Fiji. In June 2020 FCEFs findings and recommendations were published in a report and presented, separately and directly, with the Minister for Economy, the Minister for Commerce, Trade and Tourism, Transport, the Attorney-General and Minister for Economy, Civil Service and Communications, and in the National Tripartite Labour Committee. A press-release was issued and interviews with the media undertaken to share the findings. In July 2020 FCEF collaborated with the Fiji Trade Union Congress (FTUC) and Fiji Government to undertake a national tripartite COVID impact assessment and by taking advantage of its new capabilities and license for advanced data analytics and business intelligence software, was able to aggregate the new data from 271 enterprises across 9 districts into a single database to reveal additional insights on changes that had occurred over time. A national tripartite report with findings and recommendations for the COVID response and recovery plan was co-published in July 2020. FCEF published another report focusing on insights and recommendations drawn from its analysis of the aggregated data. Through the advocacy of FCEF and its effective participation in tripartite social dialogue, a number of key policy priorities and recommendations were adopted by Government and reflected in the 2020/21 national budget. One such example is the FJI$ 200 million COVID-19 Recovery Credit Guarantee Scheme that was launched by the Fiji Development Bank (FDB) as part of the 2021/22 national budget. As part of the initiative, FCEF has also been invited by the FDB to participate in the loan application review committee. In May 2020, the ILO provided assistance to FCEF for the design of surveys to assess the impact of COVID; delivered training and coaching sessions on use of the Qualtrics software for survey distribution, analysis and reporting; and supported the final analysis and report drafting. The ILO created an opportunity for FCEF to present its findings and conclusions to the Ministry of Economics for consideration in the national budget and Safe Economic Recovery Plan, and to the UN Country Office for consideration within the UNCT Fiji COVID-19 Multi-Sectoral Response Plan. In July 2020, with the support of the RBSA, the ILO provided additional training and coaching sessions on the Qualtrics software for advanced data analytics and dashboarding of findings as well as assistance for the aggregation of data and final reporting. The ILO also supported the national tripartite assessment of which FCEF participated. Further assistance to FCEF this biennium included collaboration with the ITC-ILO to provide the Chamber with customized Customer Relationship Management (CRM) software and training on its use for the secretariats membership and services unit. The CRM has helped FCEF to improve the management and enhance the efficiencies of the organization, specifically in the areas of building member relationships, to increase membership recruitment and sales of services, and professionalize its financial management. Other support includes production of a quick reference guide to common COVID response policy measures and its adaption and tailoring by the Pacific Island Private Sector Organization (PIPOS) in November 2020; trainings between December 2020 and September 2021 in partnership with the ITC-ILO on lobbying and advocacy, membership strategies, and the role of wages and productivity in pathways to sustainable recovery; and the launch of a Pacific eCampus for Pacific employers organization in May 2021.</narrative>
   </description>
